# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will look at a single simple observable:\n"
msgstr "Kita akan melihat satu observable ringkas:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "The simplest case: a fixed truncation budget for each slice {#the-simplest-case-a-fixed-truncation-budget-for-each-slice}"
msgstr "Kes paling mudah: bajet pemangkasan tetap bagi setiap hirisan {#the-simplest-case-a-fixed-truncation-budget-for-each-slice}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The available budget for truncation of Pauli terms can vary at each step of the backpropagation.\n"
"To understand how this works, we first look at the simplest case of a fixed truncation budget as specified by the user.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bajet yang tersedia untuk pemangkasan sebutan Pauli boleh berbeza pada setiap langkah perambatan balik.\n"
"Untuk memahami cara ini berfungsi, kita mula-mula melihat kes paling mudah iaitu bajet pemangkasan tetap seperti yang ditentukan oleh pengguna.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The most straightforward way to specify the truncation budget is by using the `max_error_per_slice` argument.\n"
"In fact, this is what is being done in the [Reducing depth of circuits with operator backpropagation](/tutorials/operator-back-propagation) tutorial. Setting `max_error_per_slice` to a `float` results in each slice being allotted a budget equaling that value.\n"
"In the example below, we set this value to `0.001` which guarantees an implicit truncation error of at most `0.018`, if all 18 slices were backpropagated.\n"
msgstr ""
"Cara paling mudah untuk menentukan bajet pemangkasan ialah menggunakan argumen `max_error_per_slice`.\n"
"Sebenarnya, inilah yang dilakukan dalam tutorial [Reducing depth of circuits with operator backpropagation](/tutorials/operator-back-propagation). Menetapkan `max_error_per_slice` kepada `float` menyebabkan setiap hirisan diperuntukkan bajet yang sama dengan nilai itu.\n"
"Dalam contoh di bawah, kami menetapkan nilai ini kepada `0.001` yang menjamin ralat pemangkasan tersirat paling banyak `0.018`, jika kesemua 18 hirisan dirambat balik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<div class=\"alert alert-info\">\n"
"Note that any error budget remaining after backpropagating a slice and truncating terms with small coefficients will always be added to the following slice's error budget.\n"
"</div>\n"
msgstr ""
"<div class=\"alert alert-info\">\n"
"Perhatikan bahawa sebarang baki bajet ralat selepas merambat balik sesuatu hirisan dan memangkas sebutan berpekali kecil akan sentiasa ditambah kepada bajet ralat hirisan berikutnya.\n"
"</div>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We next use the [OBPMetadata](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-obp/utils-metadata-obp-metadata) instance and the tools provided by the [visualization](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-obp/utils-visualization#module-qiskit_addon_obp.utils.visualization) module to visualize the backpropagation process.\n"
msgstr "Seterusnya kami menggunakan instance [OBPMetadata](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-obp/utils-metadata-obp-metadata) dan alat yang disediakan oleh modul [visualization](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-obp/utils-visualization#module-qiskit_addon_obp.utils.visualization) untuk menggambarkan proses perambatan balik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The top left plot** shows that we have enough budget to begin truncating observable terms after backpropagating the third slice. Starting from the third slice, we know that we truncate at least one term from each slice we backpropagate because we are incurring some truncation error after each slice.\n"
msgstr "**Plot kiri atas** menunjukkan bahawa kita mempunyai bajet yang mencukupi untuk mula memangkas sebutan observable selepas merambat balik hirisan ketiga. Bermula dari hirisan ketiga, kita tahu bahawa kita memangkas sekurang-kurangnya satu sebutan daripada setiap hirisan yang kita rambat balik kerana kita menanggung sedikit ralat pemangkasan selepas setiap hirisan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The top right plot** shows that the error budget grows to `.003` for the third slice. We see a sharp drop in remaining budget, which means terms were truncated from the observable. This is consistent with what we inferred from the top left plot.\n"
msgstr "**Plot kanan atas** menunjukkan bahawa bajet ralat meningkat kepada `.003` untuk hirisan ketiga. Kita melihat penurunan mendadak dalam baki bajet, yang bermakna sebutan telah dipangkas daripada observable. Ini selaras dengan apa yang kita simpulkan daripada plot kiri atas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The bottom left plot** shows that as we truncate terms from our observable, our overall accumulated error is growing monotonically. This graph also confirms that no terms were truncated until after the third slice had been backpropagated.\n"
msgstr "**Plot kiri bawah** menunjukkan bahawa semasa kita memangkas sebutan daripada observable kita, ralat terkumpul keseluruhan kita meningkat secara monotonik. Graf ini juga mengesahkan bahawa tiada sebutan dipangkas sehingga selepas hirisan ketiga dirambat balik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- **The bottom right plot** shows that the number of commuting Pauli groups in our observable has grown to the specified limit of `10`. This plot also shows how backpropagating one more layer would cause our observable to outgrow the specified bound as you can see from the crossover of the black and red lines.\n"
"<div class=\"alert alert-info\">\n"
"Note that in all of these plots, the x-axis enumerates the backpropagated slices, but since OBP works on the end of the circuit, `slice 1` is the very last slice, `slice 2` is the one before that, and so on.\n"
"</div>\n"
msgstr ""
"- **Plot kanan bawah** menunjukkan bahawa bilangan kumpulan Pauli commuting dalam observable kita telah meningkat sehingga had yang ditentukan iaitu `10`. Plot ini juga menunjukkan bagaimana merambat balik satu lapisan lagi akan menyebabkan observable kita melebihi had yang ditentukan seperti yang anda dapat lihat daripada persilangan garis hitam dan merah.\n"
"<div class=\"alert alert-info\">\n"
"Perhatikan bahawa dalam semua plot ini, paksi-x menyenaraikan hirisan yang dirambat balik, tetapi memandangkan OBP bekerja pada hujung litar, `slice 1` ialah hirisan paling akhir, `slice 2` ialah yang sebelumnya, dan seterusnya.\n"
"</div>\n"

