# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Specify slice budget explicitly {#specify-slice-budget-explicitly}"
msgstr "Tentukan bajet hirisan secara eksplisit {#specify-slice-budget-explicitly}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you know how to assign a budget to each slice, such that the backpropagation performance is optimized, you might want to explicitly assign a budget for each slice. For demonstration purposes, we will assign the first three slices zero budget and use a  budget of `.001` per slice for the remaining slices.\n"
msgstr "Jika anda tahu cara memperuntukkan bajet kepada setiap hirisan supaya prestasi perambatan balik dioptimumkan, anda mungkin mahu memperuntukkan bajet secara eksplisit bagi setiap hirisan. Untuk tujuan demonstrasi, kami akan memperuntukkan bajet sifar kepada tiga hirisan pertama dan menggunakan bajet `.001` bagi setiap hirisan untuk hirisan yang selebihnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Removing the budget from the first three layers resulted in no terms being truncated until after the fourth layer, as can be confirmed in three of these plots. What might be somewhat surprising is that although the fourth slice had no leftover budget passed to it, a term was still truncated by using the allocated `.001` budget. This is obvious from the **top left** plot, but can also be observed in the **top right** plot, as the leftover budget curve flattens between slices three and four. Another notable detail is that at least one term was truncated from this point on, the same as in the previous example.\n"
msgstr "Membuang bajet daripada tiga lapisan pertama menyebabkan tiada sebutan dipangkas sehingga selepas lapisan keempat, seperti yang dapat disahkan dalam tiga plot ini. Yang mungkin agak mengejutkan ialah walaupun hirisan keempat tidak mempunyai baki bajet yang disalurkan kepadanya, satu sebutan masih dipangkas dengan menggunakan bajet `.001` yang diperuntukkan. Ini jelas daripada plot **kiri atas**, tetapi juga boleh diperhatikan dalam plot **kanan atas**, kerana lengkung baki bajet mendatar antara hirisan tiga dan empat. Satu lagi perincian ketara ialah sekurang-kurangnya satu sebutan dipangkas mulai titik ini, sama seperti dalam contoh sebelumnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The key takeaway is that although we incurred less truncation error in the second example due to zeroing out some slices' budgets, we were able to backpropagate the same number of slices, and our observable contains the same number of commuting Pauli groups. We can confirm that the bound on our error is smaller in the second example by inspecting the **bottom left** plot.\n"
msgstr "Pengajaran utama ialah walaupun kita menanggung ralat pemangkasan yang lebih kecil dalam contoh kedua kerana menyifarkan bajet sesetengah hirisan, kita dapat merambat balik bilangan hirisan yang sama, dan observable kita mengandungi bilangan kumpulan Pauli commuting yang sama. Kita boleh mengesahkan bahawa had ralat kita lebih kecil dalam contoh kedua dengan memeriksa plot **kiri bawah**.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-addon-obp/guides/truncate-operator-terms/extracted-outputs/b7167f80-5d29-4c32-be97-cba733f18b1d-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-addon-obp/guides/truncate-operator-terms/extracted-outputs/b7167f80-5d29-4c32-be97-cba733f18b1d-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Specify the budget cyclically {#specify-the-budget-cyclically}"
msgstr "Tentukan bajet secara kitaran {#specify-the-budget-cyclically}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you have a circuit with some repeatable pattern, such as a Trotter circuit, you might want to specify a budget for that repeated subset of slices and have that budget used for all of the following repetitions of those slices.\n"
msgstr "Jika anda mempunyai litar dengan beberapa corak berulang, seperti litar Trotter, anda mungkin mahu menentukan bajet bagi subset hirisan yang berulang itu dan menggunakan bajet tersebut untuk semua pengulangan hirisan berikutnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "More concretely, the example circuit we are using has six slices that are repeated three times, for a total of 18 slices. We will arbitrarily assign zero budget to the single-qubit and `RYY` layers, and `.003` budget to each of the `RXX` layers. We will observe how specifying the budget as a length-6 sequence causes the budget to be applied to all 18 slices cyclically.\n"
msgstr "Lebih konkrit, litar contoh yang kita gunakan mempunyai enam hirisan yang diulang tiga kali, dengan jumlah 18 hirisan. Kami akan memperuntukkan bajet sifar secara sewenang-wenangnya kepada lapisan satu qubit dan `RYY`, dan bajet `.003` kepada setiap lapisan `RXX`. Kami akan melihat bagaimana menentukan bajet sebagai jujukan panjang-6 menyebabkan bajet diterapkan kepada kesemua 18 hirisan secara kitaran.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<div class=\"alert alert-info\">\n"
"Again, note that the slices are backpropagated in reverse order (that is, starting at the end). Therefore, the first entry in our cyclic budget actually gets used for the last slice, the second entry for the slice before that, and so on.\n"
"</div>\n"
msgstr ""
"<div class=\"alert alert-info\">\n"
"Sekali lagi, perhatikan bahawa hirisan dirambat balik dalam susunan terbalik (iaitu, bermula dari hujung). Oleh itu, entri pertama dalam bajet kitaran kita sebenarnya digunakan untuk hirisan terakhir, entri kedua untuk hirisan sebelumnya, dan seterusnya.\n"
"</div>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As seen in the **top left** and **bottom left** images, no truncation was performed over the first four slices since they were allocated no error budget. Slices five and six had some of their terms truncated as budget became available.\n"
msgstr "Seperti yang dilihat dalam imej **kiri atas** dan **kiri bawah**, tiada pemangkasan dilakukan ke atas empat hirisan pertama kerana tiada bajet ralat diperuntukkan kepadanya. Hirisan lima dan enam mempunyai sebahagian sebutannya dipangkas apabila bajet menjadi tersedia.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As seen in the **top left** image, a relatively large amount of error was incurred after backpropagating slice seven, even though that slice was allocated no budget. This is because only about `.002` of the `.006` total budget allocated to slices five and six was used, so the remaining was forwarded to slice seven and mostly expended, as seen in the **top right** image.\n"
msgstr "Seperti yang dilihat dalam imej **kiri atas**, ralat yang agak besar timbul selepas merambat balik hirisan tujuh, walaupun hirisan itu tidak diperuntukkan bajet. Ini kerana hanya kira-kira `.002` daripada jumlah bajet `.006` yang diperuntukkan kepada hirisan lima dan enam telah digunakan, jadi bakinya disalurkan kepada hirisan tujuh dan kebanyakannya dibelanjakan, seperti yang dilihat dalam imej **kanan atas**.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The **top left** and **top right** images show that the small amount of leftover budget is used up between slices 8-10, and new budget becomes available in slice 11, as expected. The **top left**, **top right**, and **bottom left** images all demonstrate the cyclical behavior of the `max_error_per_slice` argument when its length is less than the number of slices. This cyclical behavior would have continued through all the slices, but the `max_qwc_groups` stopping criteria was reached after backpropagating 13 slices, as seen in the **bottom right** image.\n"
msgstr "Imej **kiri atas** dan **kanan atas** menunjukkan bahawa baki bajet yang sedikit itu dihabiskan antara hirisan 8-10, dan bajet baharu menjadi tersedia dalam hirisan 11, seperti yang dijangkakan. Imej **kiri atas**, **kanan atas**, dan **kiri bawah** semuanya menunjukkan tingkah laku kitaran bagi argumen `max_error_per_slice` apabila panjangnya kurang daripada bilangan hirisan. Tingkah laku kitaran ini akan berterusan melalui semua hirisan, tetapi kriteria penghentian `max_qwc_groups` dicapai selepas merambat balik 13 hirisan, seperti yang dilihat dalam imej **kanan bawah**.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Also interesting is that the number of Pauli groups actually drops after the second round of budget becomes available at slice 11. This is because there were groups with small coefficients that could not be truncated until there was more budget after backpropagating slice 11, so they accumulated in the observable for several iterations. This case also highlights that `max_qwc_groups` must be _exceeded_ for the algorithm to terminate.\n"
msgstr "Menarik juga bahawa bilangan kumpulan Pauli sebenarnya menurun selepas pusingan kedua bajet menjadi tersedia pada hirisan 11. Ini kerana terdapat kumpulan berpekali kecil yang tidak dapat dipangkas sehingga ada lebih banyak bajet selepas merambat balik hirisan 11, jadi ia terkumpul dalam observable selama beberapa lelaran. Kes ini juga menonjolkan bahawa `max_qwc_groups` mesti _dilebihi_ untuk algoritma ditamatkan.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
