# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cap the total error {#cap-the-total-error}"
msgstr "Hadkan jumlah ralat {#cap-the-total-error}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In addition to specifying the per-slice error budget, one can specify the maximum amount of error to incur from truncation. Once that limit is hit, no more truncation will be performed; however, backpropagation will continue until the observable becomes too large and one of the stopping criteria is met.\n"
msgstr "Selain menentukan bajet ralat bagi setiap hirisan, anda boleh menentukan jumlah ralat maksimum yang ditanggung daripada pemangkasan. Setelah had itu dicapai, tiada lagi pemangkasan akan dilakukan; walau bagaimanapun, perambatan balik akan diteruskan sehingga observable menjadi terlalu besar dan salah satu kriteria penghentian dipenuhi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We next re-run the above experiment, setting a cap on `max_error_total` such that the error budget is expended after backpropagating slice seven.\n"
msgstr "Kami seterusnya menjalankan semula eksperimen di atas, dengan menetapkan had pada `max_error_total` supaya bajet ralat dihabiskan selepas merambat balik hirisan tujuh.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As expected, our truncation error caps out at `.006` (**bottom left** chart). It is notable that in this run we were not able to backpropagate slice 11. This is because we did not have enough budget to truncate terms and the number of commuting Pauli groups grew past the limit of `20`, as seen in the **bottom right** image.\n"
msgstr "Seperti yang dijangkakan, ralat pemangkasan kita mencapai had pada `.006` (carta **kiri bawah**). Perlu diperhatikan bahawa dalam larian ini kita tidak dapat merambat balik hirisan 11. Ini kerana kita tidak mempunyai bajet yang mencukupi untuk memangkas sebutan dan bilangan kumpulan Pauli commuting melebihi had `20`, seperti yang dilihat dalam imej **kanan bawah**.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-addon-obp/guides/truncate-operator-terms/extracted-outputs/69c9069a-9038-4319-8dc6-37a1be973ebf-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-addon-obp/guides/truncate-operator-terms/extracted-outputs/69c9069a-9038-4319-8dc6-37a1be973ebf-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It may be desirable to simply cap the overall budget with `max_error_total` without specifying `max_error_per_slice`.\n"
msgstr "Mungkin wajar untuk sekadar menghadkan bajet keseluruhan dengan `max_error_total` tanpa menentukan `max_error_per_slice`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The output of the cell above might be slightly surprising because the `per_slice_budget` is set to the `max_error_total`. This indicates that the entire available budget will be consumed **greedily**.\n"
"You can think of it this way: the entire budget is available to each slice (because we loop over the `per_slice_budget`). But any budget that has already been consumed will be deducted from the budget that is available at that given point in the algorithm.\n"
msgstr ""
"Output sel di atas mungkin agak mengejutkan kerana `per_slice_budget` ditetapkan kepada `max_error_total`. Ini menunjukkan bahawa keseluruhan bajet yang tersedia akan digunakan secara **tamak**.\n"
"Anda boleh memikirkannya begini: keseluruhan bajet tersedia untuk setiap hirisan (kerana kita membuat gelung ke atas `per_slice_budget`). Tetapi sebarang bajet yang telah digunakan akan ditolak daripada bajet yang tersedia pada titik tertentu dalam algoritma itu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The **top right** image shows how the entire `.018` error budget is made available to the first slice. No truncation is performed until the third slice, so the leftover budget remains constant. The budget monotonically decreases, as the full budget is made available to each backpropagated slice until it is expended.\n"
msgstr "Imej **kanan atas** menunjukkan bagaimana keseluruhan bajet ralat `.018` disediakan kepada hirisan pertama. Tiada pemangkasan dilakukan sehingga hirisan ketiga, jadi baki bajet kekal malar. Bajet berkurangan secara monotonik, kerana bajet penuh disediakan kepada setiap hirisan yang dirambat balik sehingga ia dihabiskan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It is notable that this experiment yielded two fewer backpropagated slices compared to the first experiment in this notebook, which is almost identical. This demonstrates that for some problems, distributing the budget evenly might be optimal. For other problems, allowing slices to greedily expend the full budget might yield better performance.\n"
msgstr "Perlu diperhatikan bahawa eksperimen ini menghasilkan dua hirisan yang dirambat balik lebih sedikit berbanding eksperimen pertama dalam notebook ini, yang hampir serupa. Ini menunjukkan bahawa bagi sesetengah masalah, mengagihkan bajet secara sekata mungkin optimum. Bagi masalah lain, membenarkan hirisan membelanjakan bajet penuh secara tamak mungkin menghasilkan prestasi yang lebih baik.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-addon-obp/guides/truncate-operator-terms/extracted-outputs/51d36d7e-0bd5-4388-bbb8-6831bf1f02e6-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-addon-obp/guides/truncate-operator-terms/extracted-outputs/51d36d7e-0bd5-4388-bbb8-6831bf1f02e6-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cap the number of backpropagated slices and the total error together {#cap-the-number-of-backpropagated-slices-and-the-total-error-together}"
msgstr "Hadkan bilangan hirisan yang dirambat balik dan jumlah ralat bersama-sama {#cap-the-number-of-backpropagated-slices-and-the-total-error-together}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you don't want to distribute their error budget all the way through the circuit but you don't want to greedily expend it either, you can specify the number of slices you intend to backpropagate (`num_slices`), along with a total error budget (`max_error_total`). This will distribute the error budget uniformly (accordingly to `p_norm`) across the input slices.\n"
msgstr "Jika anda tidak mahu mengagihkan bajet ralat anda sepanjang litar tetapi anda juga tidak mahu membelanjakannya secara tamak, anda boleh menentukan bilangan hirisan yang anda berhasrat untuk rambat balik (`num_slices`), bersama jumlah bajet ralat (`max_error_total`). Ini akan mengagihkan bajet ralat secara seragam (mengikut `p_norm`) merentasi hirisan input.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, we will cap the number of slices we might backpropagate at `12`, and we will keep the same total error budget.\n"
msgstr "Di sini, kami akan menghadkan bilangan hirisan yang mungkin kami rambat balik pada `12`, dan kami akan mengekalkan jumlah bajet ralat yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we will attempt to backpropagate the 12 slices for which we allocated some budget in the previous step. We do this by just passing in the final 12 slices in our circuit. With `p_norm=1`, each of the 12 slices has an available budget of `0.018 / num_slices = 0.0015`.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kami akan cuba merambat balik 12 hirisan yang telah kami peruntukkan sedikit bajet pada langkah sebelumnya. Kami melakukannya dengan hanya menghantar 12 hirisan terakhir dalam litar kami. Dengan `p_norm=1`, setiap satu daripada 12 hirisan mempunyai bajet tersedia sebanyak `0.018 / num_slices = 0.0015`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Since we passed a subset of our slices (in the code ``slices[-num_slices:]``) to ``backpropagate``, we must combine the slices remaining after backpropagation with the slices that were never sent for backpropagation (in the code  ``slices[:-num_slices]``).\n"
msgstr "Memandangkan kami menghantar subset hirisan kami (dalam kod ``slices[-num_slices:]``) kepada ``backpropagate``, kami mesti menggabungkan hirisan yang tinggal selepas perambatan balik dengan hirisan yang tidak pernah dihantar untuk perambatan balik (dalam kod ``slices[:-num_slices]``).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Once we have combined all of the remaining slices, we can use [combine_slices](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-utils/slicing#combine_slices) to generate the reduced-depth [QuantumCircuit](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit). Next, we inspect how many slices were backpropagated versus how large our observable became.\n"
msgstr "Setelah kita menggabungkan semua hirisan yang tinggal, kita boleh menggunakan [combine_slices](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-utils/slicing#combine_slices) untuk menjana [QuantumCircuit](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit) berkedalaman terkurang. Seterusnya, kita memeriksa berapa banyak hirisan yang dirambat balik berbanding seberapa besar observable kita menjadi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The plots show that we did successfully backpropagate all 12 slices while keeping our observable under 10 commuting Pauli groups. We can also see that using `num_slices` along with `max_error_total` results in a distribution of budgets across the slices and unused budget is again forwarded to the next slice. This is most apparent in the **top right** plot, as the budget is both expended and replenished throughout backpropagation.\n"
msgstr "Plot menunjukkan bahawa kita berjaya melakukan backpropagation pada kesemua 12 slice sambil mengekalkan observable kita di bawah 10 kumpulan Pauli yang berkomut. Kita juga dapat melihat bahawa penggunaan `num_slices` bersama `max_error_total` menghasilkan taburan bajet merentasi slice dan bajet yang tidak digunakan sekali lagi dipindahkan ke slice seterusnya. Ini paling jelas dalam plot **kanan atas**, kerana bajet digunakan dan diisi semula sepanjang backpropagation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It is notable that this method of distributing error produced the best results (more backpropagated slices), compared with the first experiment in this notebook and the example just previous this one. All of these examples allotted `.018` error budget, but backpropagation performed differently depending on how that budget was distributed.\n"
msgstr "Perlu diperhatikan bahawa kaedah pengagihan ralat ini menghasilkan keputusan terbaik (lebih banyak slice yang dibackpropagate) berbanding eksperimen pertama dalam notebook ini dan contoh sebelum ini. Semua contoh ini memperuntukkan bajet ralat `.018`, tetapi backpropagation berprestasi secara berbeza bergantung pada cara bajet itu diagihkan.\n"

