msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-addon-obp/guides/truncate-operator-terms/extracted-outputs/b0bf5050-2928-41a1-9c3d-c9d79e918f6f-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Work with multiple observables {#work-with-multiple-observables}"
msgstr "Bekerja dengan berbilang observable {#work-with-multiple-observables}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `qiskit_addon_obp.backpropagate` method allows one to pass in a sequence of observables. This simplifies the workflow when dealing with multiple target observables.\n"
msgstr "Kaedah `qiskit_addon_obp.backpropagate` membolehkan anda menghantar satu jujukan observable. Ini memudahkan aliran kerja apabila berurusan dengan berbilang observable sasaran.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We explicitly mention this here to teach you how the truncation strategy handles such a case. For the sake of this example, we add an extra observable to the one which we have been using so far:\n"
msgstr "Kami menyebutnya secara jelas di sini untuk mengajar anda bagaimana strategi pemangkasan mengendalikan kes sedemikian. Demi contoh ini, kami menambah satu observable tambahan kepada yang telah kita gunakan setakat ini:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, we repeat the first experiment from this tutorial., but with two observables to backpropagate the circuit into.\n"
msgstr "Akhir sekali, kami mengulangi eksperimen pertama daripada tutorial ini, tetapi dengan dua observable untuk backpropagate litar ke dalamnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For this example, this does not affect the number of slices that could be backpropagated. However, we can see that the two observables resulted in different numbers of Pauli terms and commuting groups.\n"
msgstr "Untuk contoh ini, ini tidak menjejaskan bilangan slice yang dapat dibackpropagate. Walau bagaimanapun, kita dapat melihat bahawa kedua-dua observable menghasilkan bilangan sebutan Pauli dan kumpulan berkomut yang berbeza.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The plots below help illustrate how the backpropagation algorithm handles multiple observables.\n"
msgstr "Plot di bawah membantu menggambarkan bagaimana algoritma backpropagation mengendalikan berbilang observable.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, the plots in the **top left**, **top right**, and **bottom left** show that the budget for truncating terms is set individually for each observable. In other words, both observables have the ability to truncate terms assuming an error of `0.001` per backpropagated slice.\n"
"Due to the different nature of the observables, this results in different consumption of the budget. In this example, they exhibit a lot of overlap, which does not always happen.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertama, plot di **kiri atas**, **kanan atas** dan **kiri bawah** menunjukkan bahawa bajet untuk memangkas sebutan ditetapkan secara individu bagi setiap observable. Dengan kata lain, kedua-dua observable mempunyai keupayaan untuk memangkas sebutan dengan mengandaikan ralat `0.001` bagi setiap slice yang dibackpropagate.\n"
"Disebabkan sifat observable yang berbeza, ini menghasilkan penggunaan bajet yang berbeza. Dalam contoh ini, kedua-duanya menunjukkan banyak pertindihan, yang tidak selalu berlaku.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The **bottom right** plot illustrates that `max_qwc_groups` takes _all_ observables into account. That means that the terms of all observables are grouped together to arrive at one final number of qubit-wise commuting groups, which is compared against `max_qwc_paulis`. The same is done for the `max_paulis` threshold (not discussed in this notebook), which allows you to set a limit on the number of Pauli terms across all observables.\n"
msgstr "Plot **kanan bawah** menggambarkan bahawa `max_qwc_groups` mengambil kira _semua_ observable. Ini bermakna sebutan semua observable dikumpulkan bersama untuk mendapatkan satu bilangan akhir kumpulan berkomut qubit-wise, yang dibandingkan dengan `max_qwc_paulis`. Perkara yang sama dilakukan untuk ambang `max_paulis` (tidak dibincangkan dalam notebook ini), yang membolehkan anda menetapkan had pada bilangan sebutan Pauli merentasi semua observable.\n"

